T(36,'The in-plane dimensions are {0} nm, exactly one pattern period. Boundaries are periodic in {1} and {2}, with no slip at the substrate and mold. A uniform volume force is imposed with acceleration {3} m s⁻². The same amplitude is used throughout the main map; the reference-geometry check is described in §2.4. OpenLB `computeU` supplies the macroscopic velocity, including the half-time-step force correction consistent with the Guo scheme. The stopping rule uses a 1000-step flux window: main-flux relative standard deviation {4}, relative range {5}, and, for principal-axis forcing, absolute cross-flux {6} m²/s. Its scope as a stopping rule, rather than an independent acceptance metric, is discussed in §3.1. Saved manifests contain binary hashes; parameters, results and logs are indexed in [Supplementary Table S1](SIM240_Supplementary_Methods_20261024/SUPPLEMENTARY_METHODS_EN_20261028.md#table-s1). Binding to historical application source, compiler configuration and OpenLB dependencies remains incomplete for some runs; this provenance limitation is retained in [S10](SIM240_Supplementary_Methods_20261024/SUPPLEMENTARY_METHODS_EN_20261028.md#sm-s10).')
