T(44,'The main map uses {0} nm. The smallest gap, {1} nm, has {2}, requiring particular attention to resolution. Refining {3} nm to 2.5 nm changes the along-groove and across-groove coefficients by approximately −0.386% and −4.431%, normalized by the 5 nm values. We therefore retain 5 nm results as references at a specified discrete resolution and report thin-gap refinement sensitivity separately. Two grids neither determine observed convergence order nor establish grid independence of the full map (§3.3).')
T(45,'Fractional wall distances are determined analytically and checked individually. All 46 analyzed cases (36 main-map, 8 refinement and 2 viscosity checks) satisfy {0} within tolerance {1}. Wall intersections therefore lie at the midpoints of neighboring-node links, so the Bouzidi rule reduces to its half-way case. This geometry-consistency check alone does not establish zero boundary error. The flat-wall convergence in Section 3 reflects the combined discretization and flux-extraction error; it does not separate those sources or establish accuracy at arbitrary fractional wall distances.')
