T(79,'**This check has a limited interpretation.** With periodic boundaries and a periodic volume force, a solution over {0} identical periods is a replication of the single-period solution by construction; resistance is mathematically independent of {1}. The check therefore tests **periodic-seam implementation and mass auditing in the enlarged domain**. It is not evidence of physical representative-volume convergence. A sufficient numerical unit cell here does not establish that a 240 nm cell represents a real device.')
T(80,'**Linearity with forcing.** The same cases give common coefficients over three forcing levels spanning a factor of four, with maximum relative differences {0} ({1} along and {2} across the grooves). This supports linear response for the reference geometry {3} nm on the 2.5 nm grid over the checked force range. Multi-force tests were not performed at all 36 main-map samples on the 5 nm grid; force independence is not claimed to have been verified sample by sample. See [S8 and Table S3](SIM240_Supplementary_Methods_20261024/SUPPLEMENTARY_METHODS_EN_20261028.md#table-s3).')
