T(163,'## 6 Conclusions')
T(164,'**1.** In the sampled 5 nm discrete results for fully filled rectangular grooves, deepening the grooves affects along-groove and across-groove transport differently. At a 50 nm gap, increasing depth from 25 to 120 nm multiplies {0} by 3.55 and {1} by only 1.034. Among gaps of 50, 75 and 125 nm covering that interval, the relative along-groove gain decreases with gap but remains approximately 39.2% at 125 nm.')
T(165,'**2.** Relative to the 5 nm discrete references, the local cubic law overestimates all 36 principal-direction samples: +10.30% to +204.85% for {0} and +8.11% to +54.19% for {1}. Along-groove discrepancy increases with depth in sampled fixed-gap sequences, but does not decrease monotonically with gap at every depth. These magnitudes and trends are not continuous-domain accuracy guarantees and identify no single dominant mechanism. Appendix E separately proves ideal-Stokes principal-conductance upper bounds, which do not determine these percentages.')
T(166,'**3.** Relative to the reference geometry’s 5 nm principal values, the model overestimates anisotropy by approximately 67%. Under the same linear tensor description, flux directions reconstructed from the two sets of principal values differ by 9.20° for forcing at 45°. These are not experimentally validated or continuous-solution-certified flow-direction errors. Both principal values and their ratio require assessment.')
T(167,'**4.** Retrospective evaluation using published V2 coefficients against 5 nm references gives maximum absolute residuals of 10.5% for 18 along-groove samples and 18.7% for 18 across-groove samples; the 15 transverse samples with {0} give 6.9%. At the transverse sample {1} nm, the absolute discrepancy increases against the 5 nm reference, and local improvement depends on the reference grid. Residual gap dependence remains. Evaluation must report sample coverage, reference grid and data-use history; the relation cannot be extended as a prediction relation for arbitrary geometries or dynamic imprinting.')
